<description>&lt;p&gt;UN peacekeepers and South Sudan authorities were accused of ignoring warnings before the Abiemnom massacre that killed at least 213 civilians, prompting Amnesty International to demand investigations. The government postponed the first national elections again, now set for February 2027, while opposition forces continue clashes with government troops in Akobo. Governors in Jonglei and Aweil East called for peace ahead of the delayed vote. An ambush on a convoy killed two people, including a journalist, and a CityLink Aviation plane crashed near Juba, killing all 14 aboard. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxPeThJckdvVVVXeHlmS2Vpem5sZFVHRUF2QmdsT3dNRjN2Sy10SVZPeTM1cTJTYVFXd3YzTnprVXZaN0o3SkljdWJDQUZHOUMtY2NFMVhSWi03WFJwLUhwbFl4bEFTTldybkl4ZWg0QzVUM2NQRGtwa2hlTEdYcGRqbWpwaWJpWS1zME05MWo3TTlFN29tdExFcnVjY0tPalZHTzFfa0ZvdjVQejEyM3BTS0JpajlfQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxPVFoxQmpwenQtQ2xaV1hlMmh1RTNUZHFwWUxMZ3d0aUpQTUgxc2FVVmZDTlBOaUF5cjAwbVRDM2ExTXEzd0poVjluRHFLdTl2ZlNLQ1RUTlM3SmgtWTB6TlV0LUlhM3V4RV8weEhSZVA3M3I3SzRZOHNIMEdlQ0hNV3hrWHVPMGxNNG5V?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxPYW42YUZhSUNjMEtPY0l1UDh2N2o1cUdFMU1WRHBnQVpNdTJCNllHT3FvSlpzSEx6cTNKS3JCOWd1OGRqVHo3UjI4dVl0ZjZhaW1iMjJnRE5rYURod3RSVFB3dDNJU1d0RS1QeDd3ZERGLW8xSEF1WENMZnZMcE9qc0JrZzNRZUlibGg2N1ZINllfelN1anFmR1F3?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href